# runner_registration_exemptions.list -- documented exceptions to the
# invariants scripts/check-runner-registration.py enforces: every test file
# tests/ci_smoke.sh actually invokes must also be invoked by
# tests/run_all.sh (what `make box-check` actually runs), because
# otherwise a box-check "green" proves nothing about a ci_smoke-only gate
# (issue #433), and every on-disk candidate test must have a runner. This
# list applies to BOTH the ci_smoke reconciliation and the orphan scan.
# A deliberate exception or recorded registration gap goes here, one per line:
#
#   filename|reason
#
# '#' comments and blank lines are ignored. No entry here means "no known
# legitimate exceptions" -- it does NOT mean the guard has nothing to check;
# run scripts/check-runner-registration.sh and read its output.
#
# The capture-smoke and uprobe ci_smoke-only gaps are fixed in run_all.sh
# (#752); neither needs an exemption. Capture smoke runs in both modes,
# with full mode gated on hardware watchpoint support as in ci_smoke.sh.
test_gesture_gate.py|Opt-in measurement harness: self-skips with exit 0 unless PGWT_RUN_GESTURE_GATE=1, and a RED verdict deliberately does not fail the run; not a pass/fail gate.
test_startup_probe_degrade.py|Recorded runner gap: covers wait-only startup degradation and requires a PG13 postmaster without pg_stat_statements in shared_preload_libraries; tests/provision-runner.sh preloads it in every gate cluster, so no provisioned runner can run it today. Follow-up #794 tracks making it runnable.
